description:
Call-off via a further competition under Crown Commercial Services RM6098 Technology Products and Associated Services 2 Framework Agreement, Lot 2 Hardware, for the provision of End User Devices (EUD) and Associated Services. 
The contract will be for an initial 4-year period with an option to extend for two further 12 months periods (4+1+1). 
The Supplier is to provide End User Devices as defined by the Council throughout the life of the contract. This will support the various worker profiles/styles of employees within the organisation. 
The Supplier is to provide an extensive and wide range of multi manufacturer enterprise/business grade EUDs and associated services including: 
• EUDs including desktops, laptops, tablets, smart phones and any other hardware that an end user can use to interact with their data and applications; 
• Product Asset Management including asset tagging, identification, utilisation reporting, addition, change and removal of assets into asset management systems via CSV or similar; 
• Product/Infrastructure Management Services including break fix, repair and upgrades; 
• Buy Back service that includes secure disposal, data wiping, refurbishing, remanufacturing and/or recycling of Hardware; and 
• Logistics, stock and warehousing solutions including delivery to end users.
Total value of awarded contract is maximum spend for definitive period of 4 years. Estimated minimum spend for definitive period of 4 years is &#xA3;3,700,000 based on minimum order quantities.

The Contracting Authority (NHS Mid and South Essex Integrated Care Board) has awarded a compliant Call-Off Contract to SOFTCAT PLC for provision of the Datix CloudIQ (DCIQ) Cloud Based software-as-a-service (SaaS) platform under the Health Trust Europe Enterprise Level Information Communication Technology (ICT) Solutions 2023 Digital Technology Framework Agreement (HTE - 011008) in accordance with the Framework Guidance and Rules. The scope of this service includes: 
-	Database to capture Incidents, Complaints, Claims, and Risk Management, retain and search legacy data from MSEICB Datix Web/Rich client systems;
-	Incident reporting system compatible with Learning from Patient Safety Events (LFPSE) Service;
-	Integrated Risk Management database that links between modules;
-	Business Intelligence functionality including dashboards for improved analysis and triangulation of system data; 
-	Fully customisable to meet current and future ICB requirements 
-	Allows for information to be reported from anywhere with internet access, from any location and device; 
-	Automated reporting;
-	Fully auditable
-	Rapid implementation; 
-	Training; and
-	Web/Cloud based in line with NHS Mid and south Essex (MSE ICB) provider organisations.


The contract commences 01st April 2026 and expires 31st March 2029 for 3 years (with break-clause at end of year 2 agreed). The aggregate contract value awarded is &#xA3;131,414.4 inc VAT. This represents &#xA3;41,685.6 for the first 12 months 01.04.2026 - 31.03.2027, &#xA3;43,770 for the second year from 01.04.2027 - 31.03.2028 and &#xA3;45,958.8 for the final year from 01.04.2028 - 31.03.2029.

This Contract Award Notice is being published in accordance with the requirements for sub-central contracting authorities, NHS Trusts and NHS Foundation Trusts where the contract value is at least &#xA3;30,000 inclusive of VAT in accordance with the Public Contract Regulations 2015, which govern the Framework Agreement his Call-Off Contract is associated with.
